@startuml
title Join waitlist for an occupied time

actor Client
participant "NGINX" as NGINX
participant "FE (Next.js)" as FE
participant "BE (Django/DRF)" as BE
database "DB (PostgreSQL)" as DB

Client -> FE : "notify me" for an occupied time
FE -> NGINX : POST /v1/availability/waitlist  (X-CSRFToken)
NGINX -> BE : proxy
note over BE
  AuthN: session; AuthZ: role = client
  availability.serializers.WaitlistJoinSerializer
  body: { service_id, desired_start_at, note }
end note
BE -> BE : availability.services.join_waitlist()
note over BE
  Business rules:
  - desired_start_at must be in the future
  - staff = service.staff (responsible staff member)
  - creates Waitlist row (status=waiting)
end note
BE -> DB : INSERT availability_waitlist
BE -> BE : notifications.notify_staff_waitlist_join()
BE -> DB : INSERT notifications_bo_alert (waitlist_join)
note right of BE
  Staff sees the alert in the BO and contacts the client
  outside the app to arrange a swap. No automatic offer in v1.
end note
BE --> FE : 201 (WaitlistSerializer)
FE --> Client : "you're on the waitlist"
@enduml
